order (root first, then children in order of original appearance). Because we push children in reverse, the first child in original order will be popped first? Wait: stack LIFO. If we push reversed, then the last child in reversed list (which is first in original) will be on top and processed first. So correct: for children [c1, c2, c3], reverse -> [c3,c2,c1]; push: push c3, then c2, then c1; then pop c1 first, so order c1, c2, c3. That's pre-order with children in original order.\n\nAlso when we encounter a node that is pruned, we do not push children, so its subtree is skipped.\n\nAt the end, retained_node_ids = retained (list in order visited). visit_order = visit_order (list of all nodes visited, including pruned ones). That matches our earlier reasoning.\n\nReturn {\"retained_node_ids\": retained, \"visit_order\": visit_order}.\n\nNow encode as JSON string in response.\n\nBut note: the output schema says additionalProperties false, but our return object only has those two keys, so fine.\n\nNow we need to output the Python source code as a JSON string.\n\nWe'll write a function decode_input? No, solve(case) receives the dict directly. So we just implement.\n\nEdge cases: Utility_threshold may be None? Not in fixtures. Node utility is float, comparison fine.\n\nMake sure to import nothing.\n\nNow produce final answer as JSON with key \"implementation\".\n\nThe implementation string must be a valid Python function definition.\n\nI'll write:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    threshold = case[\"utility_threshold\"]\n    node_by_id = {node[\"id\"]: node for node in nodes}\n    children = {}\n    root_id = None\n    for node in nodes:\n        parent = node[\"parent\"]\n        if parent is None:\n            root_id = node[\"id\"]\n        else:\n            children.setdefault(parent, []).append(node[\"id\"])\n    # DFS iterative\n    stack = [root_id]\n    visit_order = []\n    retained = []\n    while stack:\n        nid = stack.pop()\n        node = node_by_id[nid]\n        visit_order.append(nid)\n        if node[\"removable\"] and node[\"utility\"] < threshold:\n            continue\n        retained.append(nid)\n        # push children in reverse to maintain order\n        for child in reversed(children.get(nid, [])):\n            stack.append(child)\n    return {\"retained_node_ids\": retained, \"visit_order\": visit_order}\n\nThat should work.\n\nNow encode as JSON string.\n\nI need to produce a JSON object: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n\nEscape newlines as \\n, backslashes as \\\\, quotes as \\\".\n\nWe must ensure no extra text.\n\nLet's write the code as a string with proper indentation. Use 4 spaces.\n\nI'll produce the final answer."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1864,"completion_tokens":4731,"total_tokens":6595,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":4480},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1792,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":72},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}